//? Title: Fast R-CNN shared features and RoI pooling
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A region-based detector can waste most of its work repeating convolutions on overlapping image patches. This report shares a tensor backbone across proposals, checks the source bilinear RoI-pooling geometry, exposes region sampling and the full joint Adam loop, then evaluates the validation-selected detector on held-out scenes.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/fast_rcnn.cpp`.

> The method

Fast R-CNN separates image-wide convolution from per-region pooling and dense prediction. A softmax head and class-specific box head share the pooled features and a multitask objective. The compact source adaptation below uses four convolutions and bilinear14x14 sampling followed by7x7 max pooling, rather than the original large pretrained backbone and rounded RoI bins.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/fast_rcnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/fast_rcnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/fast_rcnn_concept.tikz > build/fast_rcnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/fast_rcnn_concept.svg build/fast_rcnn_concept.dvi > build/fast_rcnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
