> Simple example: one shared feature grid, many RoIs

R-CNN repeats convolution on every proposed image patch. Fast R-CNN computes a
feature map once per image and samples each region from that map. At stride s,
feature cell i has pixel centre `s*i+s/2`; a pixel edge p maps to feature coordinate
`(p-s/2)/s`, then divides by `feature_side-1` for normalized corner-aligned sampling.

The source uses bilinear `crop_and_resize` to 14x14 followed by 2x2 max pooling
to 7x7. This is an explicit adaptation of rounded-bin RoI pooling, and is not
ROIAlign. For a feature channel holding its row coordinate, the max in output
bin i selects sample `y0+(2*i+1)*(y1-y0)/13`. The same holds for columns.
Core sampling differentiates the feature map, while RoI coordinates are constants.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fast_rcnn_pooling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  const auto yy = n::arange(0, 16).reshape({16, 1}) * n::ones({16, 16}),
             xx = n::arange(0, 16).reshape({1, 16}) * n::ones({16, 16});
  const auto features = n::stack({yy, xx}, 2).reshape({1, 16, 16, 2});
  const auto rois =
      n::models::DetectionFeatureBoxes(n::tensor({8., 12., 40., 36.}, {1, 4}), 4, 16, 16);
  const auto pooled =
      n::max_pool2d(n::crop_and_resize(features, rois,
                                       n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{0}), {14, 14}),
                    2, 2, n::Padding::Valid);
  double error = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < 7; ++i)
    for (int j = 0; j < 7; ++j) {
      error =
          std::max(error, std::abs(pooled.at({0, i, j, 0}) - (1.5 + (2 * i + 1) * 8. / 13.)));
      error =
          std::max(error, std::abs(pooled.at({0, i, j, 1}) - (2.5 + (2 * j + 1) * 6. / 13.)));
    }
  if (error > 2e-6)
    return 1;
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(yy, {0}), 0, 15);
  a.title("Stride-4 feature rows")
      .x_label("feature column")
      .y_label("feature row")
      .x_limits(-.5, 15.5)
      .y_limits(-.5, 15.5);
  auto b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::slice_axis(pooled, 3, 0, 1).reshape({7, 7}), {0}),
                              0, 15);
  b.title("Seven pooled row values")
      .x_label("output bin column")
      .y_label("output bin row")
      .x_limits(-.5, 6.5)
      .y_limits(-.5, 6.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1200, 550).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/fast_rcnn_pooling.svg");
  std::print(
      "Pixels [8,40)x[12,36) map to feature rows 1.5..9.5 and columns 2.5..8.5. All 98 pooled "
      "coordinate values agree with the odd-sample maximum formula; maximum error {:.9f}.\n",
      error);
}
```
