> Scene data and foreground/background region sampling

This bounded fit uses 64 training and 16 validation scenes generated from the
first 2048 official MNIST training digits, seed 11. Eight test scenes use the
first 512 official test digits, seed 22. All scenes are 64x64, with tight boxes
above byte value 32. Classical proposals use thresholds 48, 64, 96, 128, 160,
200 and 230, including nearby component-pair unions, as in the R-CNN report.
The repeated images below show the actual truth/proposal geometry.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fast_rcnn_proposals.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  const auto images = n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 4);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> truth(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 4), proposals;
  for (int image = 0; image < 4; ++image)
    proposals.push_back(m::ComponentDetectionProposals(
        n::slice_axis(images, 0, image, image + 1).reshape({64, 64, 1}),
        {48, 64, 96, 128, 160, 200, 230}, 3));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat({m::DrawDetectionBoxes(images, truth, {.1, 1, .2}),
                                m::DrawDetectionBoxes(images, proposals, {1, .1, .1})},
                               0),
                     "build/fast_rcnn_proposals.png", 4, 0., 1., 4, 1., 2);
  std::print("Top: first four training scenes with green truth boxes. Bottom: identical "
             "pixels with all tight-threshold red proposals, including pair unions.\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Top: first four training scenes with green truth boxes. Bottom: identical pixels with all tight-threshold red proposals, including pair unions.
\image(figures/fast_rcnn_proposals.png)
// result_end
\caption(The first four actual training scenes with green truth boxes, followed by the same four images with all red classical proposals. Convolution will be shared across every region of each image.)
\alttext(The first four actual training scenes with green truth boxes, followed by the same four images with all red classical proposals. Convolution will be shared across every region of each image.)

For each training image, the tensor sampler appends ground-truth boxes and
64 random boxes, then shuffles foreground, near background and far background
separately. Foreground has IoU at least .5, near background lies in `[.1,.5)`,
and far background is below .1. It takes **up to** sixteen foreground regions,
then fills the 64-region budget with near and far background. Scarce positives
are not repeated. Tensor RNG replaces the source host RNG and has a different
sequence. Every foreground region receives box-regression targets here, unlike
R-CNN's separate .6 regression cutoff.

The gallery resamples the first twenty selected **image** regions only for
inspection. The model instead pools their shared features as shown above.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fast_rcnn_sampled_rois.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  m::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = m::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<n::Tensor> candidates;
  for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i)
    candidates.push_back(m::ComponentDetectionProposals(
        n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, i, i + 1).reshape({64, 64, 1}),
        {48, 64, 96, 128, 160, 200, 230}, 3));
  n::Generator rng(7);
  const auto batch = m::SampleDetectionRois(scenes, {0, 1}, candidates, rng);
  const auto preview = m::CropDetectionPatches(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 2),
                                               n::slice_axis(batch.indices, 0, 0, 20),
                                               n::slice_axis(batch.pixels, 0, 0, 20));
  n::save_image_grid(preview, "build/fast_rcnn_sampled_rois.png", 5, 0., 1., 4, 1., 4);
  std::print("{} sampled regions from two images; {} foreground, at most 16 per image. First "
             "twenty labels:",
             batch.labels.numel(), n::count_nonzero(batch.mask).item());
  for (auto label : n::slice_axis(batch.labels, 0, 0, 20).to_vector<int>())
    std::print(" {}", label);
  std::print(". These image crops are presentation only; the head pools features.\n");
}
