> Conclusion

The 946963-scalar model makes 256 Adam updates and selects the last epoch, 8, at
validation AP50 0.464696. On eight test scenes/23 digits, inclusive VOC AP50
is 0.603580, COCO-style AP75 is 0.295288 and AP50:95 is 0.329845, with 214
retained detections. There are
15.625 classical proposals per image; their coverage is 0.869565/0.739130
at IoU 0.5/0.7. These sparse scenes do not support an architecture ranking.

The coordinate fixture verifies shared-grid RoI pooling before fitting. Actual scene/region previews, explicit foreground/background sampling and the complete tensor optimizer loop make the data and objective inspectable. Held-out AP uses the selected detector with classical proposals only. Sharing convolution changes the computation structure; this bounded example does not claim the paper's speed or benchmark accuracy.

> References

- [Girshick (2015), Fast R-CNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.08083).
- [Girshick et al. (2014), R-CNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2524).
- [TensorFlow, crop_and_resize semantics](https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/image/crop_and_resize).
